; `begin` was the sequencing form. `{ }` replaced it, and afterwards
; `begin` was an ordinary name to the parser - so this program drew
; `AX3001 undefined variable begin`, a diagnostic that names no
; replacement and reads like a typo. Its five siblings - `union`,
; `region`, `foreign`, `linear`, `consume` - have all been reserved
; and answer AX2004 with migration advice; `begin` was the one left
; out, which `CHANGELOG.md`'s 0.2.0 Compatibility section recorded.
;
; `.axbad` because the refusal is at parse time.
(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (begin 1 2 42))
